A||||14||Black88GT||Building Off road vehicle/hybrid||||1||
Z||000000||Black88GT||10-17-2000||01:20 AM||||Just recently I was watching a movie called "Three Kings" with G. Clooney and Mark Walhberg.  I noticed they had that off road dune buggy type thing that the Army used in Desert Storm in the movie.  I thought it would be a cool project, try to make an off road type vehicle like that.  <P>I was thinking tubular frame, possibly Quad 4 engine.  I was thinking either mid-engined setup, or engine in the rear with tranny in the front.  <P>I contacted a guy who would be willing to build a tubular frame for me.  However I think I am jumping ahead of myself here since I probably won't have the money to start this project for a loooong time.<P>But anyway, what axles could I use?  I don't want it to be too big, but not small like a go-kart.  How hard would it be to put the tranny in the front?  Would this even work?  Would I need to use a radiator? I was thinking Quad 4 because its light and has nice Hp, but could I get away with possibly using a smaller 2 cycle engine?  I guess I wouldn't need too much Hp since the thing is only going to weigh like 400 lbs. with a driver, but since it is going to be off road I want a lot of power.  <P>As you can tell this is in the VERY preliminary stage, I am just trying to get some ideas/opinions...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
