Z||000005||LarryB||10-17-2000||03:09 PM||||No, what you *really* want is at<BR>  <A HREF="http://beaulieu.ne.mediaone.net:/kickhill/4wd-fiero.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://beaulieu.ne.mediaone.net:/kickhill/4wd-fiero.jpg</A> <BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously, the engine you use depends on how you're going to use the vehicle.  If you're going to drive a lot on trails or old country roads, especially during wet seasons you want a larger engine because of the low end torque and the ability for the engine to brake at lower RPMs, 2 things the Quad-4 wouldn't do very well.  Mud is like grease so brakes don't work too well on it.<p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||1
